            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 99,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Your UT doesn't show the xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Source.DevicePresence and Fan inventory items (which gets probed). Can you please test and make sure they are being exposed?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 99,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Inventory paths are shown."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "(I'm not convinced this specific commit should be held up but we should do something to fix DevicePresence overall."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, agree we should not hold the commit."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Do we need to add these to minerva_fanboard_adc_ti.json as well? Looks like thats another variant of fanboard for minerva."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "William de Abreu Pinho",
                        "email": "williamdapinho@gmail.com",
                        "username": "williamdap"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi @paligill@gmail.com, I've also added the configuration to minerva_fanboard_adc_ti.json."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/minerva_fanboard_misc.json",
                    "line": 6,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "I think FAN* is a very generic probe which might collide with others. @patrick@stwcx.xyz @amithash@meta.com Shall we go for more specific name like MinervaFan?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/minerva_fanboard_misc.json",
                    "line": 6,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes.  Quite likely to collide.\n\n@paligill@gmail.com - I think we need to fix something here with the DevicePresence code.  Even a name like \"LeakPortN\" is likely to collide in the future.  Can we do something in the device presence daemon to pull a Compatible or Manufacturer or something from the underlying device and expose it in DevicePresence also?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/minerva_fanboard_misc.json",
                    "line": 6,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "> Yes.  Quite likely to collide.\n> \n> @paligill@gmail.com - I think we need to fix something here with the DevicePresence code.  Even a name like \"LeakPortN\" is likely to collide in the future.  Can we do something in the device presence daemon to pull a Compatible or Manufacturer or something from the underlying device and expose it in DevicePresence also?\n\nYes, getting some info from the parent inventory item and exposing it via xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Source.DevicePresence interface will be good. The Name and Type will always be there for every inventory item.\n\\+ @alexander.hansen@9elements.com to look into this."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/minerva_fanboard_misc.json",
                    "line": 6,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "This patch for entity-manager\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/entity-manager/+/83062\n\nadds a `Compatible` field on `xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Source.DevicePresence` interface which is pulled from the parent inventory item."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/minerva_fanboard_misc.json",
                    "line": 6,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "The DevicePresence change is being handled as part of separate patch mentioned by Alexander above, so resolving this comment."
                }
            ],
